Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='deploy', at=datetime(2026, 10, 4, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='Deploy is a commit to the user repository by scripts/deploy.sh, and nothing else', body='*Deploy is a commit to the user repository, by `scripts/deploy.sh`, and nothing else* (2026-10-04, `docs/USERREPO-PLAN-2026-10-01.md` stage 2; the live clone and `promote.sh` are gone). The units run the app the user repository\'s `flake.lock` names (`services.suzatary.userRepo`, the one option): a store path, never a git checkout, so nothing writes under the code root, and the binary takes its code root from the unit\'s `SUZATARY_REPO` (the instance\'s `repo` names only a command line\'s checkout). `deploy.sh <rev>` resolves the rev on the branch the user flake DECLARES (asked of a mirror of it, never of Nix\'s cache: a commit of its first-parent chain, or the one publishing that source), refusing any other or one without `nix/app-input.nix`, computes the pinned lock in a scratch copy of the flake, BUILDS FIRST (`scripts/app-builds.sh`, the roots run\'s own list, from the tree that lock names, rooted under `deploy-`, with no timeout: a failed build moves nothing), runs the NEW binary\'s `verify` from its tree against the live instance (plugin manifests included, no component loaded) and its chains\' and secretary\'s stores (a refusal moves nothing: the instance changes in the same deploy, or a store is migrated first), roots the previous app\'s builds until it succeeds, writes the lock into the user repository only with its "Deploy \\<rev>" commit under safe-push\'s push lock, waits (briefly: it only links) for a `suzatary-roots` run whose `ExecMainStartTimestamp` is at or after the commit, try-restarts every running unit part of `suzatary-app.target` (the long-running units that run the app, each declared so by `servingUnit` in `nix/nixos-module.nix`) only on that run\'s `Result=success` with `roots/app` the lock\'s tree and its builds the same set at the same paths the deploy built, waits for `/api/about` to answer 200 from that app\'s builds and each restarted unit to root that app, and pushes last. Until the units restart, any failure stops a run still building, appends `Revert "Deploy <rev>"` and runs the roots again to relink the previous app, so the log never names a rev that did not run and only grows; the revert is pushed whatever its relink\'s wait does. TERM, HUP and INT are failures like any other; after the units restart a failure keeps and pushes the deploy and says to re-run it. A rollback is a deploy of an earlier rev. Committing or pushing in a dev checkout deploys nothing. Never hand-roll that wait (a stale `Result=success` took the app down 12 minutes on 2026-09-26).', rationale='Decided 2026-10-04 (docs/USERREPO-PLAN-2026-10-01.md stage 2). Incident 2026-09-26: a hand-rolled wait read a stale Result=success and took the app down 12 minutes.', supersedes=()))